        "original_id": "cc2648dd-f0f2-516d-97af-62660b663a04",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Boston Patriots, American Football League, AFL Eastern Division, Indiana University, Cleveland Browns, All-America Football Conference\n- People: Lou Saban\n- Topics: 1960 Boston Patriots season, professional football, college football\n\nFacts:\n- Lou Saban played college football for Indiana University.\n- Lou Saban played professionally for the Cleveland Browns in the All-America Football Conference from 1946 to 1949.\n- Lou Saban was the head coach of the Boston Patriots during the inaugural American Football League season in 1960.\n- The Boston Patriots finished the 1960 season with a 5–9 record.\n- The Boston Patriots finished last in the AFL Eastern Division in 1960.",
